"""29 October 2026 : ZenRay Meshes RETOPOLOGY (ZRR), the micro-component finisher : one component of the validated shape becomes
ONE clean, closed, quads-only panel whose edge loops follow its own four border curves, never the lofts nor the wrinkles of the source.
  1 view    : the component seen along its OUTWARD mean normal (visibility survey), the body rendered on the GPU at px_per_m :
              part label and depth toward the viewer for every pixel.
  2 region  : the pixels of the component, largest piece, holes filled, opened.
  3 field   : the validated shape as a FAIR height field over the plane : thin plate smoothing of the depth on a regular grid
              (cell_m), data inside the eroded region only, wavelengths shorter than fair_cut_m removed, the deviation to the
              validated shape bounded by dev_max_m (constraint based fairing, Hildebrandt and Polthier 2007, by reweighting).
  4 outline : marching squares contour of the region, four corners at its sharpest convex turns, four sides lifted on the field,
              each side a fair clamped B-spline (RigLib.fit_fair), checked by CurveFair.
  5 grid    : n_u x n_v quads from the side lengths (edge_m), borders sampled once by arc length, interior = Tutte embedding of
              the grid graph in the plane (a convex combination map is one to one when the border is convex, Tutte 1963,
              Floater 2003), heights read on the fair field : quads only, every interior vertex of valence 4, no fold.
  6 panel   : outer skin, rolled edge (half round of radius thickness / 2 in hem_steps), inner skin at thickness : one closed,
              manifold, consistently oriented, quads-only solid.
python ZrrPatch.py <component> [--edge-m 0.02] [--json overrides]       writes work/retopo/<component>/ (npz, obj, json)
FR : le finisseur de micro-composant : un composant de la forme validée devient un panneau fermé, en quads, tiré de ses bords."""
